+ ## Graduation gate
+
+ A4 graduates from shadow to active pilot when ALL of the following hold:
+
+ 1. **Low-quality decision rate** ≤ 10%: `lowQualityDecisions / auditedDecisions ≤ 0.10`.
+ 2. **Audit coverage**: every decision is audited in shadow mode (sampling rate = 1.0).
+ 3. **Budget violation response**: `degrade_to_audit_only` triggers when rate > 10% (criterion 4.14).
+ 4. **Per-turn cumulative budget**: A4 is the first to degrade (degradation order A4→A3→A5→A1).
+
+ ## A4 latency budget (documented, not measured here)
+
+ The development manual defines the A4 per-turn cumulative latency budget as
+ `p99 ≤ 300ms` over the whole turn, with the degradation order
+ A4→A3→A5→A1 (`a4` dropped before `a3`, both before `a5`, all before `a1`).
+ The order half is checkable (`tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts`); the
+ numeric A4 latency contribution is **NOT-MEASURED** in this packet because A4
+ is never executed on the production turn path.
+
+ ## Out of scope
+
+ - Post-promotion sampling (OQ-004, Stage 5).
+ - Decision quality scoring model (Stage 5 enhancement).
+
+ ## A04 re-verification (2026-11-01)
+
+ A04 re-maps the four criteria above onto executable evidence in the current
+ candidate. No threshold, sampling rule or degradation order is redefined here;
+ the pilot is not graduated, and A4 stays an offline / dev-tool-only module.
+
+ | # | Criterion (unchanged) | Evidence | Verdict |
+ |---|---|---|---|
+ | 1 | `lowQualityDecisions / auditedDecisions ≤ 0.10`, and rate > 10% → `degrade_to_audit_only` | `tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts`, `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts`, `tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts` | PASS |
+ | 2 | Audit coverage: every decision audited in shadow mode (sampling rate = 1.0) | `DecisionQualityAuditor.auditBatch` records `auditedDecisions` 1:1 with the audited records; **there is no production audit caller** (see below) | NO-GO |
+ | 3 | Budget violation response `degrade_to_audit_only` on rate > 10% | `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` (A4 branch of `checkBudgetViolation`) | PASS |
+ | 4 | Per-turn cumulative budget + degradation order A4→A3→A5→A1 | `tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts` asserts the drop order (a4, then a3, then a5, all before a1); the per-turn cumulative latency smoke never exercises A4 | Order PASS / numeric gate NOT-MEASURED (NO-GO) |
+
+ ### Criterion 2 residual: no production audit caller (NO-GO)
+
+ `DecisionQualityAuditor` records one audited decision per audited record, so the
+ in-module coverage ratio is 1:1 and no sampling is skipped. That is module-level
+ coverage only: the development manual defines A4 as *offline pure functions
+ only*, callable **ONLY via explicit dev-tool invocation** (CLI, test fixture,
+ debug panel), so there is no production audit caller and therefore no
+ production audit coverage. The original Active Pilot production gate stays
+ NO-GO; the counter evidence is not a substitute for a production audit path.
+
+ ### Criterion 4 residual: A4 latency not measured (NO-GO)
+
+ The documented degradation order (A4→A3→A5→A1) is asserted by the
+ trace-truncation drop-priority test, so A4 is the first area dropped when the
+ trace budget is exhausted. A4 is not on the production turn path, so the
+ per-turn cumulative latency smoke does not exercise it and the numeric latency
+ gate stays NOT-MEASURED (NO-GO) rather than claimed as passed.
+

